/-!
# Conditional exclusion of the extraspecial quotient in 15.3.49

`extraspecial_contradiction` excludes the actual order-27, exponent-three
alternative of 15.3.7 from the enumerated earlier local and appendix inputs.
The contained-offender proof selects a minimal eligible H, reconstructs its
faithful action, constructs an outside component and proves H = LT. Strict
span and simultaneous endpoint reversal then give a strong offender. A
contained strong best offender in the actor generated by all best offenders
supplies the final model contradictions, including the S₈ middle-node case.
The two conjugate spans always retain their different seeds:
`U_H = localSpan Z_S H` and `V_H = localSpan V H`.

In particular, bestness of either whole endpoint and generation of the first
offender span by components are not premises. The local identity
`[Z_S,O₂(H)] = Z` is proved at the selected H, using Fitting faithfulness;
the specialization at M_c alone would not suffice. All section actions and
centralizers are the literal quotients and kernels from `Actions`.

The remaining inputs and their source discharge are as follows.

* `a`, `o`, `i`, `d`, `hseed`: standing 15.3.2–12 data, the actual
  extraspecial case of 15.3.7, the 15.3.46 normalizers, uniform 15.3.48(3),
  and 15.3.49(b),(d) at the initial overgroup. `d` also retains the actual
  residual, relative theta, SQTK and centralizer-factorization assertions.
* `hseed_comm`, `hempty`, `hnormalizer`, `hlocal`, `h48`: the standing empty
  L_f and local characteristic-two hypotheses, 15.3.46(2), and all the
  needed 15.3.48(2),(3) conclusions, uniformly on eligible H below `upper`.
  `qt-15-03-fusion-coset-setup` and `qt-15-03` retain these local discharges.
* `geometry`: the conjugate actions, 15.3.49(c), the 15.3.47 normalizer
  test, F.9.13 edge-core/commutator/noncentrality, F.9.16 selection and
  F.9.17 simultaneous reversal. The edge marking is supplied at every
  endpoint that symmetric maximization can select. The actual F.9 results
  remain with `qt-f09-geometry` through `qt-f-09`; the source parent must
  construct this family from them and its earlier local conclusions.
* `classification`, `sections`, `source`: the universal adequate B.5.6,
  B.5.5(1)(iii–iv)/B.4.2 component sections, and full B.5.1 implications.
  Their existing source owners are `qt-b-05` and `qt-b-04`.
* `orbits`: the zero-two-core orbit alternative used in 1.2.1(3), retained
  by `qt-1-02-adequate-assembly`.
* `splitting`, `rank_source`: B.2.14(1) and the concrete natural-plus-dual
  rank assertion of B.4.9(2iii), retained by `qt-b-02` and `qt-b-04`.

F.9.2 and F.9.7 feed the earlier local conclusions; B.3.2 and A.3.18
enter the component/model reductions. They are not extra endpoint or model
assumptions. The earlier results must still be instantiated by the source
parent before all of 15.3.49, or the classification, is complete. The older
local-algebra and rank-comparison interfaces remain publicly available.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), printed
pp.1142–1145; F.9.13–17, pp.322–324; B.2.14, p.78; B.4.9(2iii), p.92;
B.5.1 and B.5.3–6, pp.99–105. This theorem is the conditional contradiction,
not a numbered assertion of the still-unassembled source theorem.
-/

public section

namespace CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section03.FusionCore.ExtraspecialElimination

open Subgroup ContainedOffenderRoute ContainedOffenderRoute.ReducedModels
open ComponentReduction.ModelReduction.BinaryModels
open CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section04.LocalSetup.TwoFactors.FFBranch.ClassificationComparison.FFAlternatives
open scoped IsMulCommutative commutatorElement

universe u v
variable {G : Type u} [Group G] [Finite G]

/-- The complete conditional contradiction for the extraspecial alternative
of 15.3.7. `d.extraspecial` asserts the actual order-27 exponent-three quotient
and its source centralizer/residual identities. All remaining hypotheses are
the earlier implications enumerated above; the proof constructs the minimal
local group, both contained offenders, its component, and every terminal
model/point transport internally. -/
theorem extraspecial_contradiction
    {κ : GroupClass.{u}} (T : Sylow 2 G) (M Y Y0 ZS upper : Subgroup G)
    [IsElementaryAbelian 2 (localModule T M)]
    (a : Section03.NaturalOrthogonalAction M (localModule T M))
    (o : FusionCore.NaturalOrthogonalAction M (localModule T M))
    (i : OrthogonalPlaneIndex)
    (d : EarlierLocal κ M Y (localModule T M) Y0 ZS (centralInvolutions T) upper T)
    (hseed : ZS = fixedPlane (localModule T M) (planeStabilizer T (a.plane i)))
    (hseed_comm : ⁅ZS, (T : Subgroup G)⁆ ≤ centralInvolutions T)
    (hempty : MainForward.faithfulLocalComponents T = ∅)
    (hnormalizer : ∀ W : Subgroup G, W ≤ localModule T M →
      ¬ IsTotallySingular o.form W → normalizer (W : Set G) ≤ M)
    (hlocal : ∀ H : Subgroup G, H ∈ outsideFamily Y0 (T : Subgroup G) M → H ≤ upper →
      centralizer (pCore 2 H : Set H) ≤ pCore 2 H)
    (h48 : ∀ H : Subgroup G, H ∈ outsideFamily Y0 (T : Subgroup G) M → H ≤ upper →
      localSpan (ZS.subgroupOf H) ⊤ ≤ pCore 2 H ∧
      (frattini (localSpan (ZS.subgroupOf H) ⊤)).map
        (localSpan (ZS.subgroupOf H) ⊤).subtype ≤ (centralInvolutions T).subgroupOf H ∧
      (∀ h : H, (∀ u ∈ localSpan (ZS.subgroupOf H) ⊤,
        ⁅u,h⁆ ∈ (centralInvolutions T).subgroupOf H) ↔ h ∈ pCore 2 H) ∧
      ⁅localSpan ZS H, localTwoCore H⁆ ≤ centralInvolutions T)
    (ι : Subgroup G → Type v) [∀ H, Finite (ι H)]
    (geometry : ∀ H : Subgroup G, H ∈ outsideFamily Y0 (T : Subgroup G) M →
      (hHU : H ≤ upper) →
      letI := d.elementary_seed H hHU
      letI := d.elementary_span H hHU
      Nonempty (GeometricFamily (ι H) Y (T : Subgroup G) H (localModule T M) ZS
        (centralInvolutions T)))
    (classification : ProjectiveLine.AdequateGeneralClassificationInput.{u,u} κ)
    (sections : EarlierComponentSections κ)
    (orbits : OrbitClosure.EarlierOrbitAlternative κ)
    (source : ProjectiveLine.QuasisimpleClassificationInput.{u,u} κ)
    (splitting : CharacteristicTwo.RankOneConfiguration.EightGeometry.NaturalModule.FixedGeometry.SourceB214Splitting.{u})
    (rank_source : ModelExclusions.MiddleEight.NaturalDualBestRank) : False :=
  EarlierLocal.false_of_earlier T M Y Y0 ZS upper a o i d hseed hseed_comm
    hempty hnormalizer hlocal h48 ι geometry classification sections orbits source
    splitting rank_source

end CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section03.FusionCore.ExtraspecialElimination
